Package: breedtools
Title: Design, Analysis and 'Breedbase' Storage of Plant Breeding Trials
Version: 0.1.0
Authors@R:
    person("Christiano", "Simoes", email = "ccsimoes263@gmail.com", role = c("aut", "cre"))
Description: Designs and analyses plant breeding field trials, from
    early generations with a single plot per entry to fully replicated
    trials, and saves the designs to a 'Breedbase' database. Designs:
    augmented row-column designs with replicated checks (Federer, Nair and
    Raghavarao (1975) <doi:10.2307/2529426>), including unequal row and
    column groups, incomplete blocks, extra check replication and
    D-optimal check placement (Piepho and Williams (2016)
    <doi:10.2134/agronj2016.06.0325>); multi-location augmented partially
    replicated (p-rep) designs built by search or from alpha and alpha(2)
    arrays (Williams, Piepho and Whitaker (2011) <doi:10.1002/bimj.201000102>);
    and resolvable spatial row-column designs optimized for row-column and
    linear variance efficiency, with latinized options (Williams, John and
    Whitaker (2006) <doi:10.1111/j.1541-0420.2005.00393.x>). Analyses give
    analysis of variance tables with degrees of freedom estimable from the
    observed plots and adjusted entry means with standard errors, from
    fixed models, mixed models with random blocks or random entries (best
    linear unbiased predictions), genotype-by-location interaction, spatial
    P-spline models with 'SpATS' (Rodriguez-Alvarez et al. (2018)
    <doi:10.1016/j.spasta.2017.10.003>), two-stage weighted analysis of
    multi-location trials with heterogeneous error variances (Mohring and
    Piepho (2009) <doi:10.2135/cropsci2009.02.0083>), and residual maximum
    likelihood fits of row-column, linear variance and autoregressive
    spatial models. Draws field maps, writes field books, checks designs,
    and saves designs as trials with their plots into a 'Breedbase'
    breeding program and folder through the Breeding API ('BrAPI'), and
    later the phenotypic data of those plots by plot and trait name,
    first-stage plot values as a trait and second-stage genotype values as
    a 'Breedbase' analysis. Also
    loads 'Breedbase' phenotype files, checks residual variance homogeneity
    across environments with Hartley's Fmax test (Hartley (1950)
    <doi:10.1093/biomet/37.3-4.308>), and groups environments by
    genotype-by-environment interaction (Lin (1982) <doi:10.1007/BF00276251>).
